[00:02.06] (Hank Williams - Fred Rose)
[00:08.36] Tonight down here in the valley
[00:14.16] I'm lonesome and oh, how I feel
[00:22.40] As I sit here alone in my cabin
[00:29.76] I can see your mansion on the hill.
[00:38.06] Do you recall when we parted
[00:44.24] The story to me you revealed
[00:52.02] You said you could live without love dear
[00:59.42] In your loveless mansion on the hill.
[01:17.66] --- Instrumental ---
[01:22.56] I've waited all through the years love
[01:28.46] To give you a heart true and real
[01:36.28] 'Cause I know you're living in sorrow
[01:43.96] In your loveless mansion on the hill.
[01:51.46] The light shines bright from your window
[01:58.94] The trees stand so lonesome and still
[02:06.56] I know you're alone with your pride dear
[02:13.62] In your loveless mansion on the hill...
